100 REM  ****************************************************
110 REM  *   C H I P - 8   I N   A B C   B A S I C   I I    *
120 REM  *   FOR THE ABC80 WITH THE ABC800 INTERPRETER      *
130 REM  ****************************************************
132 REM  THIS IS THE BASIC II-80 VERSION. IT HAS NO SETDOT,
134 REM  CLRDOT OR DOT, SO THE SPRITE CODE AT 5240 SETS THE
136 REM  MOSAIC BITS IN THE SCREEN MEMORY AT 31744 ITSELF,
138 REM  THE CLOCK IS THE TICK COUNTER AT 65525, AND THE KEY
139 REM  COMES FROM KEYFLG AND LASTKY AT 65506 AND 65507.
140 REM  DISPLAY: THE CHIP-8 SCREEN IS 64*32 PIXELS. THAT IS
150 REM  32*11 SEMIGRAPHIC CELLS, SO IT FITS THE 78*72 DOT
160 REM  RASTER WITH ROOM TO SPARE. TEXT ROWS 1-11 ARE PUT
170 REM  IN GRAPHIC MODE BY THE CHR$(151) IN COLUMN 0 (BASIC II
175 REM  DROPS CHR$(23) BEFORE IT REACHES THE SCREEN).
180 REM  DOT COLUMNS 0 AND 1 ARE EATEN BY THAT CONTROL CHAR,
190 REM  WHICH IS WHY X0% IS NEVER LESS THAN 2.
200 REM
210 REM  --- STORAGE -------------------------------------
220 REM  M%()  4K OF CHIP-8 MEMORY. ON A 16K MACHINE SET
230 REM        M9%=2047% ON LINE 240 AND KEEP THE ROM SMALL.
240 M9%=4095%
242 DIM M%(4096%),V%(15%),S%(15%),K%(127%),H%(255%),Q%(7%)
244 REM  M9% IS THE ADDRESS MASK; M%() IS DIMMED ONE LARGER
246 REM  SO THAT A PC AT THE VERY TOP CAN STILL FETCH TWO
248 REM  BYTES. CHANGE BOTH TOGETHER OR NEITHER.
250 REM  H%() IS N/16 AND Q%() IS THE BIT MASKS, PRECOMPUTED
260 REM  BECAUSE BASIC HAS NO SHIFTS AND DIVISION IS SLOW.
270 FOR J%=0% TO 255% : H%(J%)=INT(J%/16%) : NEXT J%
280 Q%(0%)=128%
290 FOR J%=1% TO 7% : Q%(J%)=INT(Q%(J%-1%)/2%) : NEXT J%
292 REM  R7%(T) IS THE SCREEN ADDRESS OF DOT ROW T'S TEXT ROW,
293 REM  R8%(T) TWICE THE ROW INSIDE THE CELL, X7%(R) THE TEXT
294 REM  COLUMN OF DOT COLUMN R, B7%() THE SIX MOSAIC BITS.
295 DIM R7%(35%),R8%(35%),X7%(79%),B7%(5%)
296 FOR J%=0% TO 35% : E%=J%/3% : R7%(J%)=31744%+(E% AND 7%)*128%+(E%/8%)*40%
297 R8%(J%)=(J%-3%*E%)*2% : NEXT J%
298 FOR J%=0% TO 79% : X7%(J%)=J%/2% : NEXT J%
299 B7%(0%)=1% : B7%(1%)=2% : B7%(2%)=4% : B7%(3%)=8% : B7%(4%)=16% : B7%(5%)=64%
300 REM
310 REM  --- KEYPAD --------------------------------------
320 REM  THE CHIP-8 HEX PAD MAPPED ONTO THE LEFT OF THE ABC
330 REM  KEYBOARD.  K%(ASCII) GIVES THE HEX KEY, OR -1.
340 REM      1 2 3 C        1 2 3 4
350 REM      4 5 6 D   <--  Q W E R
360 REM      7 8 9 E        A S D F
370 REM      A 0 B F        Z X C V
380 FOR J%=0% TO 127% : K%(J%)=-1% : NEXT J%
390 K1$="X123QWEASDZC4RFV"
400 FOR J%=1% TO 16% : K%(ASC(MID$(K1$,J%,1%)))=J%-1% : NEXT J%
410 REM
420 REM  --- LOAD FONT AND PROGRAM -----------------------
430 REM  THE 16 HEX DIGIT SPRITES LIVE AT 0, WHERE FX29
440 REM  EXPECTS THEM. THE PROGRAM IS LOADED AT 512.
450 FOR J%=0% TO 79% : READ E% : M%(J%)=E% : NEXT J%
460 J%=512%
470 READ E% : IF E%<0% GOTO 500
475 IF J%>M9% ; "ROM DOES NOT FIT" : STOP
480 M%(J%)=E% : J%=J%+1%
490 GOTO 470
500 REM
510 REM  --- MACHINE STATE -------------------------------
520 P%=512%  : REM  PROGRAM COUNTER
530 I%=0%    : REM  INDEX REGISTER
540 S1%=-1%  : REM  STACK POINTER
550 D%=0%    : REM  DELAY TIMER
560 S2%=0%   : REM  SOUND TIMER
570 Z%=-1%   : REM  HEX KEY BEING HELD, -1 = NONE
581 REM  BASIC II COUNTS THE 50 HZ NMI IN TICKS AT 65525
582 REM  ($FFF5), UPWARDS.  THE LOW BYTE ALONE WRAPS ONLY
584 REM  EVERY 5.12 S, LONGER THAN ANY CHIP-8 TIMER RUNS, SO
585 REM  ONE PEEK DOES.  65525 MUST STAY A FLOATING LITERAL:
586 REM  AN INTEGER STOPS AT 32767 AND CANNOT HOLD IT.
588 C9%=-1%  : REM  -1% = CLOCK PRESENT, 0% = NONE
589 C1%=0% : IF C9% C1%=PEEK(65525)
590 FOR J%=0% TO 15% : V%(J%)=0% : NEXT J%
600 RANDOMIZE
610 REM
620 REM  --- SCREEN --------------------------------------
630 X0%=8% : Y0%=3%  : REM  WHERE PIXEL 0,0 LANDS ON THE RASTER
640 ; CHR$(12%)
650 FOR J%=1% TO 11% : ; CUR(J%,0%)CHR$(151%); : NEXT J%
660 ; CUR(0%,4%)"CHIP-8 ON ABC80";
670 ; CUR(13%,0%)"KEYPAD  1234 QWER ASDF ZXCV";
680 ; CUR(14%,0%)"GAME    MINI LIGHTS OUT (TOBIASVL, CC0)";
685 ; CUR(15%,0%)"START   ANY KEY";
690 ; CUR(16%,0%)"STOP    CTRL-C";
700 OUT 6%,0%
720 REM
1000 REM  ==================================================
1010 REM  MAIN LOOP: FETCH, DECODE, DISPATCH
1020 REM  ==================================================
1030 B%=M%(P%) : C%=M%(P%+1%) : P%=(P%+2%) AND M9%
1040 O%=H%(B%) : X%=B% AND 15% : Y%=H%(C%) : N%=C% AND 15%
1050 A%=X%*256%+C%
1060 GOSUB 1200
1065 REM  TIMERS.  WITH A CLOCK THEY FALL AT A TRUE 50 HZ
1067 REM  NO MATTER HOW FAST BASIC RUNS; WITHOUT ONE THEY
1069 REM  FALL ONCE PER INSTRUCTION, WHICH IS ONLY A GUESS.
1070 E%=1%
1075 IF C9%=0% GOTO 1100
1080 C2%=PEEK(65525) : E%=(C2%-C1%) AND 255%
1085 IF E%=0% GOTO 1130
1090 C1%=C2%
1100 IF D%>0% D%=D%-E% : IF D%<0% D%=0%
1110 IF S2%=0% GOTO 1130
1120 S2%=S2%-E% : IF S2%<1% S2%=0% : OUT 6%,0%
1130 IF O%>7% GOTO 1150
1140 ON O%+1% GOTO 2000,2100,2200,2300,2400,2500,2600,2700
1150 ON O%-7% GOTO 2800,2900,3000,3100,3200,3300,3400,3500
1160 REM
1200 REM  --- KEYBOARD ------------------------------------
1210 REM  THE KEY INTERRUPT PUTS EACH KEY IN LASTKY (65507)
1220 REM  AND SETS BIT 7 OF KEYFLG (65506).  INP(56) ONLY HAS
1230 REM  BIT 7 WHILE THE KEY IS DOWN, WHICH BASIC II IS TOO
1235 REM  SLOW TO CATCH.  A KEY COUNTS AS HELD FOR THE NEXT
1240 REM  64 INSTRUCTIONS; KEY REPEAT KEEPS IT HELD.
1250 IF PEEK(65506) AND 128% THEN 1260
1252 Z%=-1% : IF Z8%>0% Z8%=Z8%-1% : Z%=Z9%
1254 RETURN
1260 E%=PEEK(65507) AND 127% : POKE 65506,0%
1270 IF (E%>96%) AND (E%<123%) E%=E%-32%
1280 Z%=K%(E%) : Z9%=Z% : Z8%=64%
1290 RETURN
1330 REM
2000 REM  --- 0NNN ----------------------------------------
2010 IF C%=224% GOSUB 5000 : GOTO 1030
2020 IF C%=238% P%=S%(S1%) : S1%=S1%-1%
2030 GOTO 1030
2100 REM  --- 1NNN  JP NNN --------------------------------
2110 P%=A% : GOTO 1030
2200 REM  --- 2NNN  CALL NNN ------------------------------
2210 S1%=S1%+1% : S%(S1%)=P% : P%=A% : GOTO 1030
2300 REM  --- 3XNN  SKIP IF VX = NN -----------------------
2310 IF V%(X%)=C% P%=P%+2%
2320 GOTO 1030
2400 REM  --- 4XNN  SKIP IF VX <> NN ----------------------
2410 IF V%(X%)<>C% P%=P%+2%
2420 GOTO 1030
2500 REM  --- 5XY0  SKIP IF VX = VY -----------------------
2510 IF V%(X%)=V%(Y%) P%=P%+2%
2520 GOTO 1030
2600 REM  --- 6XNN  VX = NN -------------------------------
2610 V%(X%)=C% : GOTO 1030
2700 REM  --- 7XNN  VX = VX + NN (NO CARRY) ---------------
2710 E%=V%(X%)+C% : IF E%>255% E%=E%-256%
2720 V%(X%)=E% : GOTO 1030
2800 REM  --- 8XYN  ARITHMETIC ----------------------------
2805 REM  ONLY N = 0..7 AND N = 14 MEAN ANYTHING
2810 IF N%>7% GOTO 2815
2812 ON N%+1% GOTO 2820,2830,2840,2850,2860,2870,2880,2890
2815 IF N%=14% GOTO 2895
2817 GOTO 1030
2820 V%(X%)=V%(Y%) : GOTO 1030
2830 V%(X%)=V%(X%) OR V%(Y%) : GOTO 1030
2840 V%(X%)=V%(X%) AND V%(Y%) : GOTO 1030
2850 V%(X%)=V%(X%) XOR V%(Y%) : GOTO 1030
2860 REM  8XY4  ADD, VF = CARRY
2865 E%=V%(X%)+V%(Y%) : G1%=0% : IF E%>255% E%=E%-256% : G1%=1%
2867 V%(X%)=E% : V%(15%)=G1% : GOTO 1030
2870 REM  8XY5  SUB, VF = NOT BORROW
2875 E%=V%(X%)-V%(Y%) : G1%=1% : IF E%<0% E%=E%+256% : G1%=0%
2877 V%(X%)=E% : V%(15%)=G1% : GOTO 1030
2880 REM  8XY6  SHIFT RIGHT. AS ON THE COSMAC VIP AND IN
2885 REM  OCTO, VX = VY SHIFTED, WHICH THE CC0 GAMES EXPECT.
2887 G1%=V%(Y%) AND 1% : V%(X%)=V%(Y%)/2% : V%(15%)=G1% : GOTO 1030
2890 REM  8XY7  VX = VY - VX
2893 E%=V%(Y%)-V%(X%) : G1%=1% : IF E%<0% E%=E%+256% : G1%=0%
2894 V%(X%)=E% : V%(15%)=G1% : GOTO 1030
2895 REM  8XYE  SHIFT LEFT
2897 G1%=0% : IF V%(Y%)>127% G1%=1%
2898 E%=V%(Y%)*2% : IF E%>255% E%=E%-256%
2899 V%(X%)=E% : V%(15%)=G1% : GOTO 1030
2900 REM  --- 9XY0  SKIP IF VX <> VY ----------------------
2910 IF V%(X%)<>V%(Y%) P%=P%+2%
2920 GOTO 1030
3000 REM  --- ANNN  I = NNN -------------------------------
3010 I%=A% : GOTO 1030
3100 REM  --- BNNN  JP V0 + NNN ---------------------------
3110 P%=(A%+V%(0%)) AND M9% : GOTO 1030
3200 REM  --- CXNN  VX = RANDOM AND NN --------------------
3210 V%(X%)=INT(RND*256%) AND C% : GOTO 1030
3300 REM  --- DXYN  DRAW SPRITE ---------------------------
3310 GOSUB 5100 : GOTO 1030
3400 REM  --- EX9E / EXA1  KEY SKIPS ----------------------
3410 IF (C%=158%) AND (Z%=V%(X%)) P%=P%+2%
3420 IF (C%=161%) AND (Z%<>V%(X%)) P%=P%+2%
3430 GOTO 1030
3500 REM  --- FXNN ----------------------------------------
3510 IF C%=7% V%(X%)=D% : GOTO 1030
3520 IF C%=10% GOSUB 5300 : GOTO 1030
3530 IF C%=21% D%=V%(X%) : GOTO 1030
3540 IF C%=24% GOTO 3610
3550 IF C%=30% I%=(I%+V%(X%)) AND M9% : GOTO 1030
3560 IF C%=41% I%=V%(X%)*5% : GOTO 1030
3570 IF C%=51% GOSUB 5400 : GOTO 1030
3580 IF C%=85% GOTO 5500
3590 IF C%=101% GOTO 5600
3600 GOTO 1030
3610 REM  FX18  SOUND TIMER. OUT 6 DRIVES THE SN76477.
3620 S2%=V%(X%) : IF S2%>0% OUT 6%,9%
3630 GOTO 1030
5000 REM  ==================================================
5010 REM  00E0  CLEAR THE CHIP-8 SCREEN
5020 REM  IN GRAPHIC MODE A SPACE IS THE EMPTY MOSAIC CELL,
5030 REM  SO 11 PRINTS BEAT 2048 CLRDOTS BY A LONG WAY.
5040 FOR J%=1% TO 11% : ; CUR(J%,4%)SPACE$(32%); : NEXT J%
5050 RETURN
5100 REM  ==================================================
5110 REM  DXYN  XOR AN N-BYTE SPRITE IN AT VX,VY.
5120 REM  VF IS SET IF ANY LIT PIXEL GETS TURNED OFF.
5130 REM  SPRITES CLIP AT THE EDGES RATHER THAN WRAPPING,
5140 REM  SO THE LOOP BOUNDS ARE TRIMMED UP FRONT.
5150 V%(15%)=0% : IF N%=0% RETURN
5160 W%=V%(X%) AND 63% : U%=V%(Y%) AND 31%
5170 L1%=N%-1% : IF U%+L1%>31% L1%=31%-U%
5180 G1%=7% : IF W%+7%>63% G1%=63%-W%
5190 FOR L%=0% TO L1%
5200 E%=M%((I%+L%) AND M9%) : IF E%=0% GOTO 5260
5210 T1%=U%+L%+Y0%
5220 FOR G%=0% TO G1%
5230 IF (E% AND Q%(G%))=0% GOTO 5250
5235 R1%=W%+G%+X0%
5237 A1%=R7%(T1%)+X7%(R1%) : B1%=B7%(R8%(T1%)+(R1% AND 1%))
5240 IF PEEK(A1%) AND B1% POKE A1%,PEEK(A1%) XOR B1% : V%(15%)=1% : GOTO 5250
5245 POKE A1%,PEEK(A1%) OR B1%
5250 NEXT G%
5260 NEXT L%
5270 RETURN
5300 REM  ==================================================
5310 REM  FX0A  BLOCK UNTIL A KEYPAD KEY IS PRESSED
5320 REM  (KEYFLG, AS AT 1250)
5330 IF (PEEK(65506) AND 128%)=0% GOTO 5330
5340 E%=PEEK(65507) AND 127% : POKE 65506,0% : IF (E%>96%) AND (E%<123%) E%=E%-32%
5360 IF K%(E%)<0% GOTO 5330
5370 V%(X%)=K%(E%) : Z%=-1%
5380 RETURN
5400 REM  ==================================================
5410 REM  FX33  VX AS THREE DECIMAL DIGITS AT I
5420 E%=V%(X%)
5430 M%(I%)=INT(E%/100%)
5440 M%((I%+1%) AND M9%)=INT(E%/10%)-10%*INT(E%/100%)
5450 M%((I%+2%) AND M9%)=E%-10%*INT(E%/10%)
5460 RETURN
5500 REM  ==================================================
5510 REM  FX55  STORE V0..VX AT I.  I ADVANCES BY X+1 AS ON
5520 REM  THE COSMAC VIP AND IN OCTO.
5530 FOR J%=0% TO X% : M%((I%+J%) AND M9%)=V%(J%) : NEXT J%
5540 I%=(I%+X%+1%) AND M9% : GOTO 1030
5600 REM  ==================================================
5610 REM  FX65  LOAD V0..VX FROM I
5620 FOR J%=0% TO X% : V%(J%)=M%((I%+J%) AND M9%) : NEXT J%
5630 I%=(I%+X%+1%) AND M9% : GOTO 1030
